# Admin Portal Rules

- React + TypeScript.
- Protected routes must block unauthenticated users.
- Navigation visibility may be permission-aware, but backend authorization remains mandatory.
- Destructive actions require confirmation.
- Sensitive fields/actions must respect role permissions.
- Use reusable table/form/modal/confirmation primitives.
- Always implement loading, empty, validation and error states.
- Do not duplicate customer authentication behavior in the admin portal.
- Add component/unit tests for new behavior.
